# LOCAL EDIT (see third_party/policy/VERSIONS.md): upstream declares each pattern
# below as `filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text`. This repo has no LFS store, so a
# vendored LFS filter is a clone-breaking trap, not a feature -- any matching file
# committed here becomes a 130-byte pointer to an object no server has, and every
# clone made with git-lfs installed then dies in the smudge filter. `binary`
# (= -diff -merge -text) keeps the intent that these are opaque blobs.
*.memmap binary
*.stl binary
*.safetensors binary
*.mp4 binary
*.arrow binary
*.json !text !filter !merge !diff
tests/artifacts/cameras/*.png binary
*.bag binary
